From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] keep.d: do not keep the sing-box binary across sysupgrade

sysupgrade puts every file listed in /lib/upgrade/keep.d into the
backup, whether it belongs to the firmware or not. /usr/bin/sing-box is
in the firmware image when the image is built with sing-box, so the
binary of the old firmware (tens of MiB) went into every backup and was
restored into the overlay over the sing-box of the new firmware: after
a flash with kept settings the old sing-box kept running, and the
overlay held a second copy of it.

/usr/bin/sing-box and /usr/lib/libcronet.so (used only with that
binary) are no longer kept. The cores installed on the router itself
are kept as before: /usr/bin/tachyon-core, its init script and the
variant marker in /etc/tachyon.

diff --git a/tachyon/files/lib/upgrade/keep.d/tachyon b/tachyon/files/lib/upgrade/keep.d/tachyon
index 359c4e07..5569f53d 100644
--- a/tachyon/files/lib/upgrade/keep.d/tachyon
+++ b/tachyon/files/lib/upgrade/keep.d/tachyon
@@ -5,7 +5,5 @@
 /etc/init.d/tachyon-core
 /etc/init.d/steer
 /usr/bin/tachyon-core
-/usr/bin/sing-box
-/usr/lib/libcronet.so
 /usr/sbin/steer
 /usr/sbin/steer-nfqws
